</STYLE>

<DIV id=seed_2 class=hc-wrap>
<DIV class=hc-eyebrow>&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV class=hc-h1>Set CPU Utilization to 20% (Single Core)</DIV>
<DIV class=hc-rule style="HEIGHT: 3px; WIDTH: 851px">&nbsp;</DIV>
<DIV class=hc-lead><FONT color=#000000>Sets the BigFix client to use up to 20 percent of one CPU core so it works faster. WorkIdle becomes 100 and SleepIdle becomes 400.</FONT></DIV>
<DIV class=hc-banner>
<DIV class=hc-bannerhd>READ BEFORE YOU RUN</DIV>
<TABLE style="WIDTH: 830px; BORDER-COLLAPSE: collapse; TABLE-LAYOUT: fixed">
<TBODY>
<TR>
<TD style="WIDTH: 50%; VERTICAL-ALIGN: top; PADDING-BOTTOM: 4px; PADDING-TOP: 3px; PADDING-LEFT: 0px; PADDING-RIGHT: 12px">
<DIV class=hc-bcell style="BORDER-LEFT: #17707f 3px solid"><B>Master Operators only</B><SPAN>If SAML is enabled, use a local BigFix MO account.</SPAN></DIV></TD>
<TD style="WIDTH: 50%; VERTICAL-ALIGN: top; PADDING-BOTTOM: 4px; PADDING-TOP: 3px; PADDING-LEFT: 12px; PADDING-RIGHT: 0px">
<DIV class=hc-bcell style="BORDER-LEFT: #17707f 3px solid"><B>Always relevant</B><SPAN>Relevance is TRUE. Target the action deliberately.</SPAN></DIV></TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD style="WIDTH: 50%; VERTICAL-ALIGN: top; PADDING-BOTTOM: 4px; PADDING-TOP: 3px; PADDING-LEFT: 0px; PADDING-RIGHT: 12px">
<DIV class=hc-bcell style="BORDER-LEFT: #17707f 3px solid"><B>Skips locked clients</B><SPAN>The action stops on clients where the action lock is set.</SPAN></DIV></TD>
<TD style="WIDTH: 50%; VERTICAL-ALIGN: top; PADDING-BOTTOM: 4px; PADDING-TOP: 3px; PADDING-LEFT: 12px; PADDING-RIGHT: 0px">
<DIV class=hc-bcell style="BORDER-LEFT: #17707f 3px solid"><B>Per core figure</B><SPAN>On four cores the total impact is about 5 percent. On eight cores it is about 2.5 percent.</SPAN></DIV></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV>
<DIV class=hc-body style="BORDER-TOP: #dce6f0 1px solid; MARGIN-TOP: 6px; PADDING-TOP: 8px">
<DIV class=hc-sec>Description</DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 6px"><FONT color=#000000 size=2>The client is designed to use 1 to 2 percent of CPU on average. The settings apply to the processor the agent runs on, so on a multi-core computer the total is divided by the number of cores. With WorkIdle 100 and SleepIdle 400 on four cores the total is [100 / (100 + 400)] / 4, which is 5 percent.</FONT></DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT color=#000000 size=2>The first action sets <TT>_BESClient_Resource_WorkIdle</TT> to 100 and <TT>_BESClient_Resource_SleepIdle</TT> to 400. The second action opens the client settings reference.</FONT></DIV>
<DIV class=hc-sec>Deployment Notes</DIV>
<UL>
<LI><FONT color=#000000 size=2>This task can only be run by Master Operators.</FONT> 
<LI><FONT color=#000000 size=2>Relevance is always true. Target the action at the computers that should use more CPU.</FONT> 
<LI><FONT color=#000000 size=2>BigFix 11.0.7 is expected to add a setting for CPU use on multi-core systems. Details are not yet available.</FONT> </LI>
</UL></DIV>
<DIV class=hc-sec>Supported Platforms</DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT color=#000000 size=2>All BigFix client platforms.</FONT></DIV><BR>
<DIV class=hc-sec>Version and Release Notes</DIV>
<DIV style="FONT-SIZE: 14px"><FONT color=#000000 size=2>1.0 - Initial version.</FONT></DIV><script> document.body.ontakeaction = function(event) {
     if (event.contentID == 'Action5') {
         if (EvaluateRelevance('master flag of current console user') === "False") {
             alert('<?jxlat Only Master Operators can run this Task.?>');
             return false;
         }
     }
 }
</script> </DIV>]]></Description>
		<Relevance>(if exists property "in proxy agent context" then ( not in proxy agent context ) else true )</Relevance>
		<Relevance>TRUE</Relevance>
		<Category>BigFix Master Class</Category>
		<DownloadSize>0</DownloadSize>
		<Source>HCL BigFix AVP and Professional Services</Source>
		<SourceID></SourceID>
		<SourceReleaseDate>2026-09-29</SourceReleaseDate>
		<SourceSeverity></SourceSeverity>
		<CVENames></CVENames>
		<SANSID></SANSID>
		<MIMEField>
			<Name>x-fixlet-first-propagation</Name>
			<Value>Tue, 22 Jun 2004 23:25:23 +0000</Value>
		</MIMEField>
		<MIMEField>
			<Name>x-fixlet-domain_attributes</Name>
			<Value>BES Component Client</Value>
		</MIMEField>
		<MIMEField>
			<Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
			<Value>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:44:51 +0000</Value>
		</MIMEField>
		<Domain>BES </Domain>
		<Delay>PT1S</Delay>
		<Action ID="Action5">
			<Description>
				<PreLink>Click </PreLink>
				<Link>here</Link>
				<PostLink><![CDATA[ to set the BES Client to use <B>very high</B> CPU usage (&lt; 20%).]]></PostLink>
			</Description>
			<ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell">// Set CPU useage to 20% of a single core. 
// On an 4-core machine: The total system impact drops to roughly 5% total CPU.
// On an 8-core machine: The total system impact drops to roughly 2.5% total CPU.

// Note that BigFix 11.0.7 will offer a new setting to handle updating CPU use on multi-core sytems.
continue if {not locked of action lock state} 

setting "_BESClient_Resource_WorkIdle"="100" on "{parameter "action issue date" of action}" for client

setting "_BESClient_Resource_SleepIdle"="400" on "{parameter "action issue date" of action}" for client</ActionScript>
		</Action>
		<Action ID="Link6">
			<Description>
				<PreLink>Click </PreLink>
				<Link>here</Link>
				<PostLink> for more information on "_BESClient_Resource_WorkIdle", "_BESClient_Resource_SleepIdle", and other advanced BES configuration settings.</PostLink>
			</Description>
			<ActionScript MIMEType="text/x-uri">http://support.bigfix.com/bes/misc/besconfigsettings.html</ActionScript>
		</Action>
	</Task>
</BES>
